@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# AI Development Organization
+
+This directory defines the provider-neutral AI team structure for TachiyomiAT development.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Rather than relying on a single omniscient AI agent, this project uses a structured team of specialist roles. The repository filesystem is the persistent communication layer — any capable AI provider (Claude, GPT, Gemini, local models) can participate by reading the same role definitions, reports, and task history.
+
+## Directory structure
+
+```
+docs/ai_org/
+├── README.md              ← you are here
+├── roles/                 ← provider-neutral role definitions
+│   ├── repository-steward.md
+│   ├── product-lead.md
+│   ├── technical-lead.md
+│   ├── delivery-lead.md
+│   ├── reviewer.md
+│   ├── implementer.md
+│   └── design-lead.md
+└── templates/             ← lightweight task workspace templates
+    ├── task-readme.md
+    ├── status.md
+    ├── repo-health.md
+    ├── investigation.md
+    ├── delivery-plan.md
+    ├── review.md
+    ├── decision.md
+    └── implementation-verification.md
+```
+
+## Key principles
+
+1. **AGENTS.md** is for the Main Leader only. Subagents do NOT read it.
+2. Each subagent reads its own role file from `docs/ai_org/roles/`.
+3. Subagents receive only task-relevant context, not the entire project.
+4. Detailed work goes into persistent Markdown reports, not chat.
+5. The Main Leader synthesizes team output for the Director.
+6. Process must scale with risk — small tasks stay small.
+7. Provider-specific harness config is an adapter, not the source of truth.
+
+## How roles are used
+
+The Main Leader (reading `AGENTS.md`) decides which roles a task requires based on its risk level. It then delegates to specialists by pointing them to:
+- Their role file (`docs/ai_org/roles/<role>.md`)
+- The task workspace (`Plan/active/<task>/`)
+- Relevant specialist knowledge (`docs/` files)
+- Relevant source code and tests
+
+Subagents complete their work, write reports to the task workspace, and return a brief completion message. The Main Leader reads reports and synthesizes for the Director.
+
+## Evidence model
+
+Reports on consequential topics should classify key claims:
+
+| Classification | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| VERIFIED | Directly confirmed from source code, tests, measurements, or reproduction |
+| STRONG INFERENCE | Evidence strongly supports but not directly demonstrated |
+| ASSUMPTION | Reasonable but unverified |
+| UNKNOWN | Insufficient evidence |
+| CONTRADICTION | Available evidence conflicts with the claim |
+
+Use these where certainty materially affects a decision. Do not label every sentence.
+
+## Provider integration
+
+This organization is designed to work with any AI coding assistant:
+
+- **Claude Code**: Main session reads `AGENTS.md`; custom subagents read their assigned role file.
+- **Gemini/Antigravity**: Main session reads `AGENTS.md` via rules; subagents receive role file in prompt.
+- **GPT/Codex**: Same pattern — main context includes `AGENTS.md`, delegated tasks include role file.
+- **Local models**: Read the same repository files.
+
+The role file is always authoritative. Harness-specific configuration is a thin adapter.
